    "statement": "THE 512-ENTRY CAP WAS IN FORCE FOR EVERY READING BELOW AND THIS PROMOTION DID NOT CHANGE IT. ADR 0036 precondition (a) admitted a further raise as one of three responses; T020 took response 2 — split the 78-entry headroom with the one wave that is still unpromoted — so both cache caps are exactly what T018 left them. The values here are read from EXTERIOR_RUNTIME_BUDGETS in the same tree the served bundle was built from rather than typed into this record, so a reading taken at a different cap cannot be presented as a reading at this one."
  },
  "note": "T020 promotion acceptance. The PROMOTED DEFAULT COMPOSITION — Block 835 V3, Midtown-core V3, the Lower-Manhattan P1 successor, the Southern-remainder P1 successor and the Central-and-upper-Manhattan P1 successor streaming together over the pinned manhattan-citywide-20260804 base — measured in the production preview build by the shipping CesiumJS renderer, with Chrome's vsync and frame-rate limit disabled, at the UNCHANGED 512-entry cache cap. A FIVE-wave composition had never been measured before this run, which is what ADR 0036 precondition (d) required. That precondition also asked for the capped control to be captured in a second browser, for GPU texture memory to be labelled COMPUTED if it is computed, and for isolated slow frames to be STATED rather than smoothed: `cappedControl` is the reading that proves this run is uncapped, `gpuTextureArithmetic` is computed and is not measured anywhere in this file, and every station carries `worstObservedFrameMilliseconds` beside its medians.",
