      "note": "The RELEASE-TIME derivation counts GLB FILES ON DISK: 28 for Block 835 V3, which ships two LODs per building, 156 for Midtown-core V3, 71 for Lower-Manhattan P1, 179 for Southern-remainder P1 and 40 for this release. At runtime a session fetches fewer, because only the selected LOD is requested — the T016 record measured 14 Block 835 GLBs against 28 on disk — so the disk derivation is CONSERVATIVE rather than wrong, and `worstObserved` above is what this session actually made resident. An immutable release must be sized against the release-time number, which is why both are recorded. ADR 0034's admissible response 3 — counting RESOLVED entries rather than files on disk — was considered at T020 and REJECTED: both canonical levels of detail of Block 835 can be resident in one session under ordinary camera movement, so a resolved count would understate real occupancy by exactly the amount that matters. The 38 entries left are two more than the 36 this promotion's split RESERVED for wave w05, so a T022 promotion that fits its reservation fits this cache without another cap change."
